 budget violations, the local government is under scrutiny. Despite efforts to resolve these problems, town leaders believe dissolution might be necessary for long-term viability. Residents may face changes to services currently provided due to the dissolution process.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-town-founded-in-1907-has-voted-to-begin-dissolving-itself-after-years-of-financial-trouble-ronda-could-lose-its-municipal-status-by-june-2027-and-become-part-of-unincorporated-wilkes-county/articleshow/134439102.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-town-founded-in-1907-has-voted-to-begin-dissolving-itself-after-years-of-financial-trouble-ronda-could-lose-its-municipal-status-by-june-2027-and-become-part-of-unincorporated-wilkes-county/articleshow/134439102.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T20:04:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134439269,imgsize-1230802.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pat Boone’s Beverly Hills home, bought for $159,000 in 1960, is now asking nearly $23 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134439842.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pat Boone and his late wife Shirley bought a Beverly Hills estate for $159,000 in 1960. The property is now on the market for $22.95 million after significant appreciation in real estate values. The estate features a six-bedroom residence and a guest house on 1.12 acres. Boone has decided to sell the property after living there for more than six decades.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1960-pat-boone-paid-159000-for-a-1939-beverly-hills-estate-later-adding-a-guest-house-and-turning-an-open-air-patio-into-a-rec-ro